  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "After a bit of a misunderstanding today, I realized that it would be nice to have account creation date listed in the client and on the website.\n\nThis came from thinking that a certain infamous VRChat user was unbanned, when really he just made a new account with the same name as one of his old accounts. (Edit: Apparently what I heard is actually at least partially true, but that's not relevant to this and what I'm saying here stands).\n\nThis led to some rumors of him being unbanned, and some understandable outrage, up until someone used VRCX to check the account creation date.\n\nThing is, you shouldn't need VRCX to check for this info. I personally uninstalled VRCX long ago for personal reasons (being able to see who has unfriended me is toxic to me mentally, I actually prefer that information to be kept out of my reach).\n\nSo yeah, my argument is that account creation date is sometimes useful information and shouldn't require a third-party API tool to take a glance at.\n\nDiscord recently added account creation dates to profiles and I don't think it should be surprising to anyone if VRC was to do the same.\n\nThanks.",
